---
// The published KrisFlyer Saver ladder, indexed to economy.
//
// This is the single most load-bearing exhibit in the piece, and it is entirely
// a fact about a published chart: no fare, no valuation, no forecast. Singapore
// Airlines prices a business award at roughly two to two and a half times the
// economy award, and a First/Suites award at about three times. Revenue
// management does not price cash tickets on anything like that ladder, and the
// gap between the two ladders is the whole reason premium-cabin redemptions
// return more per mile.
//
// Figures: one-way Saver awards from Singapore, chart effective 1 November 2025.
// Cross-checked across two independent transcriptions of Singapore Airlines'
// award chart, with the pre- and post-devaluation deltas reconciling against
// The MileLion's separately reported percentage changes. Verified 12 Aug 2026.
import { Font } from 'astro:assets';
import ToolBrand from '../ToolBrand.astro';

// Miles are printed by SIA in thousands; stored here in full miles.
const ZONES = [
  { zone: 5,  label: 'Beijing, Shanghai',          y: 20500, j: 45000,  f: 61500  },
  { zone: 8,  label: 'Perth, Darwin',              y: 20500, j: 42500,  f: 60500  },
  { zone: 9,  label: 'Australia (others), NZ',     y: 29000, j: 72000,  f: 98000  },
  { zone: 10, label: 'Africa, Middle East, Turkey',y: 32000, j: 68000,  f: 95000  },
  { zone: 11, label: 'Europe',                     y: 44000, j: 108500, f: 148000 },
];

const rows = ZONES.map((z) => ({
  ...z,
  jx: z.j / z.y,
  fx: z.f / z.y,
}));

const maxMiles = Math.max(...rows.map((r) => r.f));
const jxLo = Math.min(...rows.map((r) => r.jx));
const jxHi = Math.max(...rows.map((r) => r.jx));
const fxLo = Math.min(...rows.map((r) => r.fx));
const fxHi = Math.max(...rows.map((r) => r.fx));

const n = (v: number) => v.toLocaleString('en-SG');
const x = (v: number) => v.toFixed(2) + '×';
---

<Font cssVariable="--font-mono" />

<div class="cl">
  <div class="cl-head">
    <span class="cl-lbl">The published ladder &mdash; one-way Saver awards from Singapore</span>
    <span class="cl-lbl accent">Chart effective 1 Nov 2025</span>
  </div>

  <p class="cl-preset">Every figure below is the award chart, not an estimate. The multiples are
  the point: a business award costs <b>{x(jxLo)}&ndash;{x(jxHi)}</b> the economy award, and a
  First or Suites award <b>{x(fxLo)}&ndash;{x(fxHi)}</b>. Hold that ladder in mind, then price
  the same three cabins in cash on any long-haul route you like.</p>

  <div class="cl-rows">
    {rows.map((r) => (
      <div class="cl-row">
        <div class="cl-zone">
          <b>Zone {r.zone}</b><em>{r.label}</em>
        </div>
        <div class="cl-bars">
          <div class="cl-bar">
            <div class="cl-bar-l"><span>Economy</span><b class="num">{n(r.y)}<i>1.00&times;</i></b></div>
            <div class="cl-track"><div class="cl-fill y" style={`width:${(r.y / maxMiles) * 100}%`}></div></div>
          </div>
          <div class="cl-bar">
            <div class="cl-bar-l"><span>Business</span><b class="num">{n(r.j)}<i>{x(r.jx)}</i></b></div>
            <div class="cl-track"><div class="cl-fill j" style={`width:${(r.j / maxMiles) * 100}%`}></div></div>
          </div>
          <div class="cl-bar">
            <div class="cl-bar-l"><span>First / Suites</span><b class="num">{n(r.f)}<i>{x(r.fx)}</i></b></div>
            <div class="cl-track"><div class="cl-fill f" style={`width:${(r.f / maxMiles) * 100}%`}></div></div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    ))}
  </div>

  <div class="cl-out">
    {/* Keep "a <b>" on one line: a line break between text and an element is
        collapsed away in .astro templates, which fuses the two words. */}
    <div class="cl-out-s">The award chart is a <b>published ladder</b>. The fare table is
    a <b>revenue-management decision</b>, remade daily, and on long-haul it separates the cabins by
    far more than these multiples do. A mile does not know which cabin it is buying &mdash; which
    is precisely why the cabin you point it at decides what it is worth.</div>
  </div>

  <div class="cl-notes">
    <p><b>What this is.</b> Singapore Airlines' own one-way Saver award pricing from Singapore,
    for five zones chosen because they carry the redemptions discussed in this piece. Premium
    economy is omitted from the ladder for legibility, not for judgement.</p>
    <p><b>What it is not.</b> A claim about availability. Saver seats are the cheapest rung and
    the scarcest &mdash; a published price you cannot book is worth nothing, and no chart shows
    you how many seats sit behind each number.</p>
    <ToolBrand />
  </div>
</div>

<style is:global>
.cl{
  --cl-bd:var(--color-border); --cl-t1:var(--color-dark); --cl-t2:var(--color-body);
  --cl-t3:var(--color-muted); --cl-deep:var(--color-navy);
  --cl-mono:var(--font-mono),'SF Mono',Menlo,Consolas,monospace;
  background:#fff;border:1px solid var(--cl-bd);border-radius:12px;
  box-shadow:0 4px 6px rgba(0,0,0,.05),0 2px 4px rgba(0,0,0,.04);
  overflow:hidden;margin:26px 0;font-size:16px;line-height:1.6;color:var(--cl-t1)
}
.cl .num{font-family:var(--cl-mono);font-variant-numeric:tabular-nums}
.cl-head{padding:14px 22px;background:var(--color-surface);border-bottom:1px solid var(--cl-bd);
  display:flex;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center;gap:12px;flex-wrap:wrap}
.cl-lbl{font-size:11px;font-weight:700;text-transform:uppercase;letter-spacing:1px;color:var(--cl-t3)}
.cl-lbl.accent{color:var(--color-brand-700)}
.post-content .cl-preset{font-size:12.5px;color:var(--cl-t3);line-height:1.55;
  margin:0;padding:12px 22px;border-bottom:1px dashed var(--cl-bd)}
.cl-preset b{color:var(--cl-t2);font-weight:600}

.cl-rows{padding:6px 22px 16px}
.cl-row{padding:14px 0;border-bottom:1px dashed var(--cl-bd)}
.cl-row:last-child{border-bottom:none}
.cl-zone{margin-bottom:9px}
.cl-zone b{font-size:13px;font-weight:700;color:var(--cl-t1)}
.cl-zone em{font-style:normal;font-size:12.5px;color:var(--cl-t3);margin-left:8px}
.cl-bars{display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:9px}
.cl-bar-l{display:flex;justify-content:space-between;align-items:baseline;gap:12px;margin-bottom:4px}
.cl-bar-l span{font-size:13px;color:var(--cl-t2)}
.cl-bar-l b{font-family:var(--cl-mono);font-size:14px;font-weight:600;color:var(--cl-t1)}
.cl-bar-l i{font-style:normal;font-family:var(--font-body);font-size:11px;font-weight:700;
  color:var(--cl-t3);margin-left:8px}
.cl-track{height:9px;background:var(--color-surface-alt);border-radius:999px;overflow:hidden}
.cl-fill{height:100%;border-radius:999px;min-width:2px}
.cl-fill.y{background:#B9C4D2}
.cl-fill.j{background:var(--color-brand-600)}
.cl-fill.f{background:#9C7526}

.cl-out{background:var(--cl-deep);color:#fff;padding:17px 22px}
.cl-out-s{font-size:15px;line-height:1.6;color:#D8DEE8}
.cl-out-s b{font-weight:600;color:#fff}

.cl-notes{padding:15px 22px 17px;border-top:1px solid var(--cl-bd);background:var(--color-surface)}
.post-content .cl-notes p{font-size:12.5px;line-height:1.55;color:var(--cl-t3);margin:0 0 7px}
.post-content .cl-notes p:last-child{margin-bottom:0}
.cl-notes b{color:var(--cl-t2)}
@media(max-width:640px){
  .cl-head{gap:4px}
  .cl-rows{padding:6px 16px 14px}
  .cl-bar-l span{font-size:12.5px}
}
</style>
